                <h2>Pre-Recharge Verification Checklist</h2>
<p>Before recharging accounts on platforms like Meta, Google, or TikTok, complete the following checks to avoid budget waste or account issues after topping up.</p>
<ul>
<li>[ ] <strong>Confirm account status is normal</strong>: Check if the account is suspended, restricted, or has unresolved payment issues—recharging a suspended account locks funds.</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Verify current balance</strong>: Some platforms credit immediately while others have 24-48 hour delays; avoid duplicate recharges.</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Select recharge method</strong>: Credit cards, PayPal, bank transfers, and corporate transfers have different processing speeds and fees—standardize your team's preferred method.</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Confirm currency and exchange rate</strong>: When recharge currency differs from spend currency, verify conversion rules in advance to prevent discrepancies.</li>
<li>[ ] <strong>Record transaction IDs</strong>: Assign internal reference numbers to each recharge (platform + account ID + date + amount) for later invoice and spend tracking.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Standard Spend Reconciliation Steps</h2>
<h3>Daily Verification (Recommended: Every Morning)</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Export previous day's ad spend report and cross-check with platform backend data.</li>
<li>[ ] Identify abnormal spend fluctuations (exceeding 30% of previous day requires investigation).</li>
<li>[ ] Verify that delivery, clicks, and conversions match spend amounts for active ads.</li>
<li>[ ] Record effective daily spend, excluding invalid traffic or refunds.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Weekly Verification (Recommended: Every Monday)</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Summarize weekly spend across all accounts and compare with recharge amounts to calculate balance changes.</li>
<li>[ ] Review spend distribution by campaign and ad group to identify high-spend, low-conversion placements.</li>
<li>[ ] Confirm any refunds or platform credits received during the week.</li>
<li>[ ] Update internal reconciliation sheets, marking weekly financial status (total recharged, total spent, current balance).</li>
</ul>
<h3>Monthly Verification (Recommended: 1st-5th of Each Month)</h3>
<ul>
<li>[ ] Export complete monthly spend report and reconcile with platform monthly invoices.</li>
<li>[ ] Verify platform commissions and taxes match contract terms (e.g., Google Ads service fees).</li>
<li>[ ] Check for missing invoices or mismatches between invoice amounts and actual spend.</li>
<li>[ ] Generate monthly financial summary: total recharged, total spent, total refunded, total invoiced, balance carried forward.</li>
</ul>
